    "preload_102": "hot_preload.zone3_fit_bonded_shank — `102`'s span with the Zone-3 shank's run bonded (lib.mechanics)",
    "verdict": "With a Zone-3 fit locating the flange — the CEM's Ø9 × 14 mm shank taken as fitted rigidly in the sleeve (a placeholder, HW.8.9; a fit that slips returns the bark reading) — only the 18 mm gap below the shank is PEEK, and the shank's run grows at 9.76 ppm/K as the Ti bonded to the PEEK around it (`102`'s gap-only span takes the Ti's 8.6, an offset of 0.9 ppm/K on the gap). The share of the sway shift: in state 2 capped at 0.60 ⊥ 0.10, 0.00–0.06 at the air-dry readings; in state 3 with no bearing 0.02–0.59, up to 0.65 ⊥ 0.30 at a rigid bark. Heat: over every state, bond, bearing and tie depth the gap's effective CTE never falls below 14.73 ppm/K against the 8.6 at which the pad's travel changes sign on that span, so within the model the free sleeve stays the adverse end of the pad's thermal travel — the free gap at 47.9 ppm/K, 0.9 above `102`'s gap-only reading — while xylem's CTE stays above 5.95 ppm/K (the one reading taken is 7.9); the deciding corner (a rigid tie at the thick bark's install-day cambium, 24 mm, below the shank) leaves the shank's run unloaded; the span following the wood outright takes the gap's CTE to 4.33, a reversed shift per kelvin under 10.9 % of the free sleeve's. The cold conclusion holds while the gap's CTE stays above 38.1–39.1 ppm/K and the hot one above 39.3 (the cambium-under-the-flange (`79`) reading has no hot threshold: the free sleeve does not leave the window hot there); state 2: the centre pad's cold conclusion flips not below 3324 N/mm (stiff bond); the centre pad's hot conclusion flips not below 3223 N/mm (stiff bond); Ta's seam passes k 1 with the hot preload not below 1940 N/mm (stiff bond); state 3 with no bearing, at the stiff bond: the cold one (the pad out of L1) holds only while the tie sits deeper than 23.8 mm on the capsule-edge (`90`) reading, at no depth on the cambium-under-the-flange (`79`) reading; the hot one (the pad out of L1) holds at no depth on the capsule-edge (`90`) reading (the deepest tie sits at 24 mm); at the soft bond both hold at every depth. Ta on the adverse reversed corner needs 0.55 in state 1 with `102`'s preload on the bonded shank's span, and in state 3 at least 0.93 on the sway alone and 1.18 with the preload at the stiff bond, 0.48 and 0.68 at the soft one, whatever the tie's depth and the bearing."
